  "what": "Recall@k for the genome-to-ranked-targets stage with the ICTV family as the unit of analysis, and a bootstrap interval on the lift over a hypergeometric null.",
  "why": "benchmarks/README.md states the defect this answers: 26 of the panel's genomes sit in a pattern-identical group, so an aggregate over them as independent instances is inflated, and the prescription is to combine within family first and then across families. The per-genome figure is reported beside this one and is not replaced by it.",
  "unit_of_analysis": "family",
  "weighting": "mean of family means; each family carries one vote whatever its genome count, because weighting by count reproduces the per-genome figure",
  "interval": "percentile bootstrap over FAMILIES, 10,000 draws, seeded 20261119",
  "null": "hypergeometric probability that a random ranking puts at least one matching chain in the top k, averaged within family before across families",
